1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
I see. You're making an outfit for your school's contest.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Going with a suit?

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
We're gonna be working on this one as a team.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
We're a team when we make Hina dolls, too.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
It helps to split the workload.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
It's not a solo gig?

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Well, the tasks are typically divided.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Head, clothes, hands, props, hair.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
And a different artisan puts together all the finishing touches.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
At our shop, it takes approximately ten people to complete one Hina doll.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Whoa! That's a whole squad!

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Multiple artists often work together on the same face.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Each feature is its own job.

14
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
That's seriously wild stuff.

15
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
So, like, how many Hina dolls do you apply makeup to in a day?

16
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Usually it's around two to three hundred.

17
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Stop. You're kidding, right?

18
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
On busy days, we'll do even more than that.

19
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Painting those teeny tiny faces looks so impossible.

20
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
I would have guessed you guys only knock out like ten or so when you're super locked in.

21
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Only ten?

22
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
We would never make our shipping deadlines.

23
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
I wasn't really going for funny.

24
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The only reason we're able to do it is because we have lots of help.

25
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Specialized work like this isn't the sort of thing you can do on your own.

26
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
It'll drive you nuts.

27
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
It may be easy to lend a friend a hand, but the ability to ask for help when you need it is a tricky skill to cultivate.

28
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
We must learn to rely on those around us.

29
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Right.

30
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Your girl needs seconds!

31
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
If you're booked up until the festival is over, I could do your laundry to save you some time.

32
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
That's okay. I don't want you to hurt your back again.

33
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
I'm fine. The doctor said it's as good as new.

34
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
